mechanism_details.numerical_example:
Using the MRCC expression
K_d = K_d^{0}\,exp\!\left[-\frac{S^{2}\,\hbar^{2}\,\omega_{\text{res}}^{2}}{\Delta E\,R\,T}\right]
with S = 0.30, \hbar = 1.0545718\times10^{-34}\,J·s, \omega_{\text{res}} = 5.0\times10^{13}\,s^{-1}, \Delta E = 1.6\times10^{-20}\,J, the universal gas constant R = 8.314\,J·mol^{-1}·K^{-1} and T = 298\,K, we obtain:

Numerator = S^{2}\,\hbar^{2}\,\omega_{\text{res}}^{2}
          = (0.30)^{2}\,(1.0545718\times10^{-34})^{2}\,(5.0\times10^{13})^{2}
          ≈ 2.5\times10^{-42}\,J^{2}

Denominator = \Delta E\,R\,T
            = (1.6\times10^{-20})\,(8.314)\,(298)
            ≈ 3.96\times10^{-17}\,J^{2}\,mol^{-1}

Exponent = -\frac{2.5\times10^{-42}}{3.96\times10^{-17}}
         ≈ -6.3\times10^{-26}

exp(exponent) ≈ 1 - 6.3\times10^{-26}

Therefore
K_d ≈ K_d^{0}\,(1 - 6.3\times10^{-26})
    ≈ 1.0\times10^{-6}\,M (to within 15 significant figures).
